    "text": "This is a greedy solution. It picks routers one at a time by best coverage gained per unit of cost and grows the backbone incrementally. It is written to the statement but has not been compiled or run against the real data sets, so the 10-second limit is estimated rather than measured.\n\n**Coverage.** For a router at (a, b), I walk each of the four quadrants outward row by row, i.e. as a staircase. The column reach in row offset `dr` is the minimum of the previous row's reach and the distance to the first wall in that row. This gives exact coverage in O(R\u00b2) per router with no prefix sums. Axis cells are emitted by exactly one quadrant, so nothing is counted twice.\n\n**Backbone distance.** Cables can pass through walls, so the cost to connect a cell is its Chebyshev distance to the nearest backbone cell. I keep this in a `dist` array. Whenever new backbone cells are added, an incremental breadth-first search (8 neighbours, unit steps) lowers `dist` only where it shrinks, so the array stays exact. Connecting a router is a walk down the distance gradient. The path is added in reverse order, so every listed cell comes after a neighbour that is already connected.\n\n**Greedy choice.**\n- Each candidate's key is `gain / (Pr + Pb\u00b7dist)`, and candidates sit in a max-heap.\n- I use lazy evaluation: when a candidate is popped, its gain and distance are recomputed.\n  - If its true value is still at least the next key, it is accepted.\n  - Otherwise it is pushed back with the updated key.\n- Every 50 accepted routers the heap is rebuilt. This uses the stored gains, which can only overestimate, together with current distances, so far cells do not stay stuck with outdated low keys.\n- A router is accepted only if it fits the remaining budget and `1000\u00b7gain > cost`, so every router adds to the score.\n\n**Validity.** Routers are placed only on non-wall cells that are already on the backbone. Backbone cells are listed without repeats, each after a neighbour. The budget is checked before each router is accepted.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint H, W, R;\nvector<char> wall, target;\n\ntemplate <class F>\nvoid forEachCovered(int a, int b, F f) {\n    static int lim[32];\n    for (int q = 0; q < 4; q++) {\n        int sr = (q & 1) ? -1 : 1, sc = (q & 2) ? -1 : 1;\n        int prev = R;\n        for (int dr = 0; dr <= R; dr++) {\n            int row = a + sr * dr;\n            if (row < 0 || row >= H || prev < 0) { lim[dr] = -1; prev = -1; continue; }\n            int l = -1;\n            for (int dc = 0; dc <= prev; dc++) {\n                int col = b + sc * dc;\n                if (col < 0 || col >= W || wall[row * W + col]) break;\n                l = dc;\n            }\n            lim[dr] = l; prev = l;\n        }\n        for (int dr = (sr < 0 ? 1 : 0); dr <= R; dr++) {\n            if (lim[dr] < 0) break;\n            int row = a + sr * dr;\n            for (int dc = (sc < 0 ? 1 : 0); dc <= lim[dr]; dc++) {\n                f(row * W + b + sc * dc);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long Pb, Pr, B;\n    int br, bc;\n    if (scanf(\"%d %d %d\", &H, &W, &R) != 3) return 0;\n    scanf(\"%lld %lld %lld\", &Pb, &Pr, &B);\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &br, &bc);\n    int N = H * W;\n    wall.assign(N, 0); target.assign(N, 0);\n    {\n        static char buf[2000];\n        for (int r = 0; r < H; r++) {\n            scanf(\"%s\", buf);\n            for (int c = 0; c < W; c++) {\n                char ch = buf[c];\n                if (ch == '#') wall[r * W + c] = 1;\n                else if (ch == '.') target[r * W + c] = 1;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    vector<int> dist(N);\n    for (int r = 0; r < H; r++)\n        for (int c = 0; c < W; c++)\n            dist[r * W + c] = max(abs(r - br), abs(c - bc));\n    vector<char> covered(N, 0), alive(N, 0);\n    vector<int> gain(N, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n        if (wall[i]) continue;\n        int g = 0;\n        forEachCovered(i / W, i % W, [&](int j) { g += target[j]; });\n        gain[i] = g;\n        if (g > 0) alive[i] = 1;\n    }\n    auto keyOf = [&](int i) { return (double)gain[i] / (double)(Pr + Pb * dist[i]); };\n    vector<pair<double, int>> heap;\n    auto rebuild = [&]() {\n        heap.clear();\n        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++)\n            if (alive[i]) heap.push_back({keyOf(i), i});\n        make_heap(heap.begin(), heap.end());\n    };\n    rebuild();\n\n    long long spent = 0;\n    vector<int> bbList, routers;\n    vector<int> bfsq;\n    bfsq.reserve(N);\n    int accepted = 0;\n    while (!heap.empty()) {\n        if (B - spent < Pr) break;\n        pop_heap(heap.begin(), heap.end());\n        auto [k, i] = heap.back();\n        heap.pop_back();\n        if (!alive[i]) continue;\n        int g = 0;\n        forEachCovered(i / W, i % W, [&](int j) { if (target[j] && !covered[j]) g++; });\n        gain[i] = g;\n        if (g == 0) { alive[i] = 0; continue; }\n        long long cost = Pr + Pb * (long long)dist[i];\n        if (cost > B - spent) { alive[i] = 0; continue; }\n        if (1000LL * g <= cost) { alive[i] = 0; continue; }\n        double v = (double)g / (double)cost;\n        if (!heap.empty() && v < heap.front().first - 1e-12) {\n            heap.push_back({v, i});\n            push_heap(heap.begin(), heap.end());\n            continue;\n        }\n        // accept\n        vector<int> path;\n        int cur = i;\n        while (dist[cur] > 0) {\n            path.push_back(cur);\n            int r = cur / W, c = cur % W, d = dist[cur], nxt = -1;\n            for (int dr = -1; dr <= 1 && nxt < 0; dr++)\n                for (int dc = -1; dc <= 1; dc++) {\n                    if (!dr && !dc) continue;\n                    int nr = r + dr, nc = c + dc;\n                    if (nr < 0 || nr >= H || nc < 0 || nc >= W) continue;\n                    if (dist[nr * W + nc] == d - 1) { nxt = nr * W + nc; break; }\n                }\n            cur = nxt;\n        }\n        reverse(path.begin(), path.end());\n        bfsq.clear();\n        for (int p : path) { bbList.push_back(p); dist[p] = 0; bfsq.push_back(p); }\n        for (size_t h = 0; h < bfsq.size(); h++) {\n            int u = bfsq[h];\n            int r = u / W, c = u % W, d = dist[u] + 1;\n            for (int dr = -1; dr <= 1; dr++)\n                for (int dc = -1; dc <= 1; dc++) {\n                    if (!dr && !dc) continue;\n                    int nr = r + dr, nc = c + dc;\n                    if (nr < 0 || nr >= H || nc < 0 || nc >= W) continue;\n                    int vv = nr * W + nc;\n                    if (dist[vv] > d) { dist[vv] = d; bfsq.push_back(vv); }\n                }\n        }\n        forEachCovered(i / W, i % W, [&](int j) { covered[j] = 1; });\n        routers.push_back(i);\n        alive[i] = 0;\n        spent += Pb * (long long)path.size() + Pr;\n        accepted++;\n        if (accepted % 50 == 0) rebuild();\n    }\n\n    string out;\n    out.reserve((bbList.size() + routers.size()) * 12 + 32);\n    out += to_string(bbList.size()); out += '\\n';\n    for (int p : bbList) { out += to_string(p / W); out += ' '; out += to_string(p % W); out += '\\n'; }\n    out += to_string(routers.size()); out += '\\n';\n    for (int p : routers) { out += to_string(p / W); out += ' '; out += to_string(p % W); out += '\\n'; }\n    fwrite(out.data(), 1, out.size(), stdout);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
